== Z1: eta(sigma) = sum (-1)^(n-1) n^-sigma > 0 and zeta(sigma) = eta/(1 - 2^(1-sigma)) < 0 on (0,1) ==
sigma = 0.01..0.99 (99 points): all eta > 0, all zeta < 0; max zeta on grid = -0.509291 (at sigma -> 1 it tends to -inf, at 0 to -1/2)
proof (elementary): eta(sigma) is an alternating series with decreasing terms, so 0 < 1 - 2^-sigma <= eta(sigma); and 1 - 2^(1-sigma) < 0

== Z2: solutions of n^p = n in Z/p^2 (Frobenius identity to second order) ==
p : count  -> 2:2, 3:3, 5:5, 7:7, 11:11, 13:13, 17:17, 19:19, 23:23, 29:29, 31:31, 37:37, 41:41, 43:43, 47:47, 53:53, 59:59, 61:61, 67:67, 71:71, 73:73, 79:79, 83:83, 89:89, 97:97, 101:101, 103:103, 107:107, 109:109
count == p for every p listed: True (the p Teichmuller residues; the other p^2 - p residues: order exactly 1)

