Stepanov's count over F_q has the sharp constant 1 (nu_1 <= q + O(sqrt q)); Chebyshev's auxiliary integer pays 2 log 2 = 1.386 per unit.

== Z4: finite-support Chebyshev auxiliary integers F_x = prod_k (floor(x/k)!)^{c_k}: constant kappa = A T/(T-1) > 1 ==
Chebyshev 1852 (1,-1,-1,-1,+1 at 1,2,3,5,30): A = -sum c_k log k / k = 0.921292 ; int_0^inf g t^-2 dt (cutoff) = 0.921284 ; g>=0 and g>=1 on [1,6): True ; kappa = A T/(T-1) = 1.105550 > 1
binomial C(2n,n) weights {1:1, 2:-2}: balance check - sum c_k/k = 0: True
C(2n,n) as F_x with x = 2n, weights {1:1, 2:-2}: A = log 4 / ... per unit x: 0.693147 ; g = floor(t) - 2 floor(t/2) in {0,1}, = 1 on [1,2): kappa = 2A = 1.386294
